# Follow the terminal's own 16-color palette instead of carrying a fixed theme.
# Ghostty is configured adaptively (light:Alabaster, dark:Catppuccin Mocha, see
# dot_config/ghostty/config), so any theme pinned here would be legible in one
# macOS appearance and wrong in the other. "ansi" tracks whichever is active.
--theme="ansi"

# Line numbers and git-modification marks, without the surrounding grid/header —
# keeps output pasteable.
--style="numbers,changes"
